-- HIDDEN TEXT-DIRECTION CHARACTER ---------------------------- main.kl  SEC0110

I found U+202E (RIGHT-TO-LEFT OVERRIDE). It changes how the line is displayed without changing how it compiles, which is how Trojan Source attacks work. Arabic text never needs it raw.

8│     let xs = [1, 2, 3]  # ‮reversed
                             ^

Help: Delete it. If a string really needs it, write it as an escape, `\u{...}`, so readers can see it.

Learn more: kalam explain SEC0110
